End-of-line comments stay on their statement's line, separated by
exactly two spaces whatever the source spacing (none, one, many, a tab),
and are not separately indented (fmt.indent_style). The comment text
itself is byte-identical (feature.formatting A3).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:DECLARE nA, nB, nC;
nA := 1;/*glued;
nB := 2; /* one space;
nC := 3;                     /* far away   with   inner   spacing;
:RETURN nA + nB + nC;	/* tab separated;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:DECLARE nA, nB, nC;

	nA := 1;  /*glued;
	nB := 2;  /* one space;
	nC := 3;  /* far away   with   inner   spacing;

	:RETURN nA + nB + nC;  /* tab separated;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
